{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgieThMv4VwtdBf57rR9X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's today's weather (Wednesday, 4 November) in the three cities:\n\n| | **Warsaw** | **Gdańsk** | **Wrocław** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Sky | Overcast | Light drizzle | Light drizzle |\n| Temp (min–max) | 4 – 9.5 °C | **6.6 – 10.6 °C** | 6.2 – 9.8 °C |\n| Feels like | 1.7 – 6.9 °C | **4.1 – 7.5 °C** | 3.0 – 6.4 °C |\n| Rain | 17% chance, 0 mm | 25% chance, 0.1 mm | **13% chance, 0 mm** |\n| Wind (gusts) | 13 (28) km/h | **10 (25) km/h** | 11 (27) km/h |\n| Air quality | **Poor** (AQI 67) | **Moderate** (AQI 49) | Moderate (AQI 53) |\n| Sunset | 16:01 | 16:04 | **16:21** |\n\n**Gdańsk is nicest today, but only just.** It's the warmest, the least windy and has the cleanest air. Its drizzle adds up to just 0.1 mm, so you won't need an umbrella.\n\n**Wrocław is a very close second.** It's the driest of the three, and sunset there is about 20 minutes later. Pick it if staying completely dry or having more daylight matters most.\n\n**Warsaw is last today.** It's the coldest of the three, and the air quality is poor. The advice is to avoid hard outdoor exercise there, and you might want a mask.\n\nAll three days are grey and chilly. A warm jacket and a sweater will do in every city, and none of them needs an umbrella.\n\nYour message also listed five other weather questions. I answered only the comparison you asked about. Tell me if you'd like me to answer the others too."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1599,"cache_read_input_tokens":43616,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1599},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sess